course: dictionary
lesson: 7228
title: Phrasal verbs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A phrase is a group of words that work together. A phrasal verb is a verb plus a small word, such as up, out, on, in or off. Together they make a new meaning. «A phrasal verb is a verb plus a small word like up, out, on, in or off.»
explain: You often cannot guess the meaning from the parts. «Give up» does not mean lifting something upwards. It means stop trying. Read the whole group of words, not just each word alone.
explain: One phrasal verb can have more than one meaning, so the situation decides. «Dad picking you up at 5» means collecting you in the car, not lifting you into the air. Ask yourself: what is happening here?
fact: Phrasal means made of a phrase, or to do with phrases.
fact: A phrasal verb is a verb plus a small word, such as up, out, on, in, off, away or down.
fact: The small word is called a particle.
fact: Together, the verb and particle can make a new meaning. «Give up» means stop trying.
fact: One phrasal verb can have several meanings, so check the sentence around it.
exercise: In «She did not give up.», which small word is the particle? | not | *up | did | she
exercise: «I will look after your pet while you are away.» What does "look after" mean? | Look behind it | Stare at it | Walk past it | *Take care of it
exercise: «Dad picking you up at 5» means what? | Dancing with you | Lifting you into the air | *Collecting you in the car | Dropping you off at school
test: «The lights went out at midnight.» Here, "went out" means the lights stopped shining. | Left the house for a party | *Stopped shining, so it was dark | Walked outside into the garden | Turned into a bright colour
test: Which group of words is a phrasal verb? | Yellow | Gentle | Quickly | *Get up
exam: Which statement about phrasal verbs is true? | A particle is a type of noun | *Their meaning can differ from their parts, so you must check the situation | Phrasal verbs are only used in science | Their meaning is always the sum of their parts
